corrected_recommendation:
Test partial in a separate Etapa C test variant and keep production on enabled until a test plate passes inspection. The code supports partial: at v02.08.02.60, partial only skips the neighbour-layer infill intersection (PrintObject.cpp:1944-1947 and :1975-1978). It keeps the 6+1-layer top projection, the 3-layer bottom projection and the small solid areas from minimum_sparse_infill_area. The thing removed is the narrow solid strip behind the walls on slopes (printed as 'Floating vertical shell'). Those strips are slow: 33k segments with a median of 0.22 mm, plus 2562 travels.

How to build the test: python3 -I ferramentas/gerar_variante_3mf.py variantes/Jogos_Vorazes_producao_4pecas.3mf variantes/Jogos_Vorazes_producao_4pecas_evst_partial.3mf --processo ensure_vertical_shell_thickness=partial. The result has "ensure_vertical_shell_thickness": "partial" and different_settings_to_system[0] = "default_acceleration;enable_support;ensure_vertical_shell_thickness;seam_position;wall_generator". Change nothing else. Keep sparse infill at 15% gyroid and infill_combination=0 for this first test, so that any change in the surface can be traced to this setting.

Expected result: about -3 to -6 min per piece, central about -4 min, or about 5-10% of the ~57-60 min per piece Bambu Studio estimates for 4-up.

After slicing, check:
- the config block reads "; ensure_vertical_shell_thickness = partial";
- FVS + ISI + Bridge volume falls from 1035 mm³ to roughly 250-450 mm³ (if it stays above about 500, the gain is small);
- FVS in Z 12-48 drops to under about 25% of today's 7.1 m, without needing to be zero;
- Z 0-4 internal solid infill (about 1.0 m) and Z 48-64 internal solid infill (0.5-0.8 m per band) stay.

Print-check under raking light, against the reference piece:
- ring shoulders and bird body, Z 32-52;
- inside of the hole, Z 8-24;
- head tops, Z 56-64.

Use the existing walls-plus-gyroid band at Z 20-28 as the control. If gyroid shows through or the shine changes, go back to enabled. Do not add a third wall to compensate.
